WEBVTT

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.540
I'm sorry,

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.990
but I can't go with you.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.760
You keep telling us to run, but to where?

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.250
There is no safe haven for us.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.750
Well...

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.450
I truly appreciate that you came for me.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.260
But the path has not yet opened for us.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.020
Thank you, but the time to try our luck isn't now.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.940
Is it because of the snow?

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.470
Lieselotte, you may not go.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.970
It is your punishment for betraying the Magius.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:29.560
It was no betrayal. I merely wished to remain honest.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.750
Their target is Module 77?!

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.190
That's right.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:11.620
The space-capable Phantom is headed for the moon.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.690
But the moon is a neutral area!

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.670
Remember how JIOR was also neutral? Yeah.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.800
We have to go back to the Moon! Module 77 is defenseless!

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.120
We still haven't met up with JIOR yet!

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.680
And we still need to find Rukino!

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.930
But what's it all worth if we don't have a home to return to?

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.100
You're right, but still...

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.270
What do we do now, L-Elf?

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.030
I have a plan.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.030
The royalists included some intel along with their supplies.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.660
What's that?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.790
A rocket?

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.920
You only see those on the history channel nowadays.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.210
It's an old multi-stage rocket from the last century.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.420
You want to use that rusty firecracker?

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.730
That is precisely why the Dorssian army will overlook it.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.280
And one more thing.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.430
Those are all JIORian names.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.300
These are the names of the JIORians who have been deported to the town we're headed for.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.310
If we rescue them, we'll have a general idea of how things are going in JIOR.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.790
And that certainly works for a show of force, too.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.080
But...

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.450
It depends on who all of these people are.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.210
It doesn't matter why. We still gotta save them.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.330
What's wrong?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.920
My dad's name's there!

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:31.880
Are you serious?!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:32.790
There!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.460
Do you know anyone else?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.540
My dad?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.440
My mom?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.560
My grandpa?

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:40.680
Is this the whole list?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.350
Wait, this name...

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.400
It's not here...

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.210
There might be family members of those who stayed on the Moon.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.080
That's right!

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.210
Let's look!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.440
I'm sorry to bother you with this.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:06.950
The little I can do to help while stuck within this cage brings me solace.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.260
What is this permit for?

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.080
Are you helping a deserter?

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:18.580
Or someone related to the royal family?

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:20.590
JIORians, actually.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.960
The students who came down to Earth.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.340
What if—

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.490
Is there an issue with that?

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.350
No, not at all.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.860
Mikhail...

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:53.870
You know, H-Neun was leaking military intel and stuff.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:04.170
It's not like he didn't have it coming.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.460
"Do not allow traitors to live." Remember?

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.680
I'd have taken him out myself if had I known.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.580
This city looks very old, but it's still beautiful.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.590
Dorssiana was the capital of the Dorssian Empire for a thousand years after all.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.940
For a thousand years?

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:48.590
The people must've held the royalty dear.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:53.350
But in the coup a decade ago, most of them were incarcerated.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.960
<i>On the famous Red Thursday,</i>

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:01.690
<i>Dorssia turned into a military state that aggressively expanded.</i>

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:05.610
<i>This district turned into a ghost town,</i>

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.010
<i>but the royalists know it like the back of their hands.</i>

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.240
They're here.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.380
They fell for it.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.730
Here's your opportunity.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.190
You get to see your dad.
Isn't that great?

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:48.570
But...

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.180
Don't hold back for us.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.570
You can be happy.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.630
That's not it.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:57.280
I've hardly ever seen my father.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.830
He was really busy with work. He barely ever came home.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.150
He was a researcher at some pharmaceutical company. He's really smart.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:14.340
That might be why I was a bit wary of talking to him.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.830
I was scared I'd let him down.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.850
But now, I think I'll be able to look at him in the eye.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.380
Hm, looks good to me. Let's give it a try.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.180
Agreed.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.440
Oh, what's that?

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:59.180
Ah, him? Tokishima Haruto, my son.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.710
But that's...

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:07.310
He makes me so proud.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.910
Is something wrong?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.840
Prepare for combat.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.800
Central security lines infiltrated.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.750
Address: Kaiserberg 672.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.310
D-5421.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.620
The exhibition is now closing.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:52.570
All visitors, please proceed to the nearest exit.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.840
The museum's main systems...

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.400
Down a few layers...

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.010
The exhibit area... Camera.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:16.710
There's Akira's signal.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.560
As soon as Haruto's team comes back, we're leaving.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.340
Let's do this.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.250
So you were a royalist too, Kriemhild?

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.750
Your ability to see in the dark always astounded me.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:55.960
Do you know her?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:57.380
My former superior.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.470
The deported JIORians are held underground.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.170
We can take you to the entrance of the duct.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:04.640
You've got two hours.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.750
Understood.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.640
You won't ask why I betrayed Dorssia?

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:14.550
I wish my life were so easygoing that I could trust the words that came out of your mouth.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.900
My men will guide you to the duct.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.190
Very well.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.900
Let's get moving right away.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.820
On an unrelated note,

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.040
is there anyone called Mikhail among you?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.570
No, no one.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:35.290
That isn't a JIORian name.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.100
I see. Forget I asked.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.870
Wait.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.930
When I entered the Karlstein Institute, they took my name.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:52.020
They gave me the identification code L-11, that is L-Elf.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.940
Don't tell me it's you...

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.300
The gate to this hangar has the seven dragons insignia.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.070
That means it's for royalty use.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.950
L-Elf, it's in your best interest not to dig too deep.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:07.530
To use it, you need approval from someone in the line of succession to the throne.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:10.640
That narrows it to a list of 63 people.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:14.460
56 of those are confirmed not to be in Dorssia.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:18.650
That leaves us with a list of seven you could have gotten approval from.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.970
And among those seven the only one who knows my former name

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.340
is her.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.070
Her?

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:26.800
The girl on the photo?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.680
Stop it!

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:33.880
My pre-Karlstein name. The seven dragons on the gate. The line of succession to the throne.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.440
It all leads to one thing.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:43.650
Hey!

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.280
L-Elf, stop!

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:51.660
What do we do, Major?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.360
What was that about?! What about the plan?

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:57.220
It's too dangerous without L-Elf. Let's follow him.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:57.850
No.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.860
We stick to the plan.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:00.670
Tokishima?

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.000
You want to go on without L-Elf?

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.760
We'll fight our own fight.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.220
Just as we want to see our family and protect our friends,

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:12.770
he has his own reasons to fight as well.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.300
We're quite deep underground.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.990
She said it goes down 100 meters.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.140
Does that indicate they're important?

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.640
They brought them all the way here from JIOR too.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:35.910
No way! My dad's just a white-collar worker!

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:08.650
Ship number DS-HUW40768S254.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.310
This is the one L-Elf's kids stole.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:14.660
It isn't just students we're facing.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.240
L-Elf might be here, too.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:21.040
You seem to be wary of him, Captain.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.600
That should tell you just how dangerous he is.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:26.150
Yes, sir.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.430
I'll storm the bridge.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.950
You open the hangar.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:31.160
Blitzendegen!

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:42.530
Is this the spot where we're supposed to meet up?

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:43.980
Supposedly.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.630
It's pretty cold.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.660
Um, who are you?

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.990
Are you from JIOR?

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:56.370
Yes. We're here to rescue you.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.540
Help came!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.000
Just like she said it would!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.870
She was telling the truth!

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.040
We can go home now!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.360
I've been dreaming of this day!

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:05.390
Excuse me!

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:07.960
Is there a Tokishima Soichi among you?

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.760
Huh? Tokishima?

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.760
Yes. Tokishima Soichi's my father.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.560
I see.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.120
Are you those...

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.820
...kids who fight the world?

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.710
Fate... or more like causality?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:24.400
Hey!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.740
Causality?

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:28.510
Tokishima, I didn't tell you yet, but—

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:33.310
Haruto! Haruto, I'm so glad you made it!

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.440
Dorrsian weather must've been hard for you!

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:36.350
Dad?

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:40.950
How are you feeling? Hurt anywhere?

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.930
Stop that, Dad!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:43.800
Let me see!

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.700
I'm fine! I'm not a kid anymore!

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.800
That tickles, Dad!

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.560
Ah, sorry.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.570
It's been a while.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:55.600
Three years?

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:01.850
Yeah! But there hasn't been a day I didn't think of you!

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.110
I have your photo on my desk.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:07.530
My photo?

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.560
I've been watching you.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.860
I'm so proud of you, Haruto.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.370
Look at it!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.520
Aren't you handsome, Haruto?

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.370
This is you!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.880
What's that?

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:29.880
Your gene map, my greatest creation!

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:33.630
You won't find a sequence more beautiful in the entire world!

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:35.100
Dad?

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:39.430
Dr. Tokishima was in charge of the VVV Project.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.520
But you said you worked for a pharmaceutical company.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:47.210
Ah, I lied.

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:50.860
The VVV Project is a state secret.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.280
It was a camouflage.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.570
Then you were making weapons?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:57.660
Tools of murder?!

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:02.570
Weapons? The Valvraves aren't something barbaric like that!

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:08.350
We just decorated them with weapons and armor because the army was sponsoring it.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:13.550
With the Valvraves, we are trying to create a new lifeform!

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:19.050
That's right! You've surpassed humanity!

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.370
The rulers of all mankind—

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:26.560
no, of the universe, the second generation of primates, has arrived.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:37.700
You're all special, chosen ones adjusted for the VVV project!

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:42.000
Adjusted? What project?

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.910
A project to develop the Valvraves and their pilots.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:52.490
You were all born with your genes and runes adjusted for the Valvraves.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.130
Who let this happen?!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.880
We got consent.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.260
I don't remember giving you mine!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:02.920
What a silly thing to say. How could you have given your consent before being born?

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.640
Your parents authorized this, of course.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.290
No! I was tricked!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.400
I... I was a dreamer...

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.030
In the end, it didn't stop you from cooperating.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.340
I don't want to hear any criticism from you.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:20.950
The children of the VVV project members are not only experiment subjects, but also hostages.

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:24.020
Genius, isn't it? Two birds with one stone.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:30.790
<i>I must find the others and warn them about the enemy.</i>

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:39.300
No one's here? What's going on?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.480
L-Elf...

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:47.310
I've found the transport L-Elf stole 30 kilometers east of Dorssia in a forest.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.390
No one was aboard.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:56.440
If they've abandoned that ship, that means they've found some other means of transportation.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:19:00.880
They need something big enough to carry the Valvraves.

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:04.450
Something large, and civilian...

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:08.960
It must be this base!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.210
I see. That's not a bad conclusion.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.930
Q-Vier, taking off!

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.380
Blitzendegen!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.380
I don't recall giving you any orders.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:24.570
Let's consider other possibilities.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:28.140
They may have secured themselves the aid of the royalists.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:32.510
Or even the royal family itself.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.370
Now they're gonna blast away the tower wall.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.320
L-Elf was caught?!

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.360
Don't worry, Haruto.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:58.640
You're a special being blessed by science.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.760
Not even the Dorssians could kill you.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.590
"Blessed"?!

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.400
This is a curse!

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:08.440
We lose our memories, our soul, and live by consuming the lives of others!

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:12.130
The second generation of primates stands at the top of the food chain.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:16.020
Just as humans eat pigs and fish, that's a perfectly natural thing to do—

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:16.730
Dad!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:22.250
Stand proud, Haruto! You're the ultimate being!

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.430
Wait, but since I gave birth to you,

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:29.980
does that make me a god in a scientific sense?

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.630
Tokishima, that's enough...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:41.210
Haruto?

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.770
Ultimate being, my ass!

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.420
Too many died for that!

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:51.200
Aina, Marie, and so many JIORians.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:56.770
Don't worry, Haruto. As a second generation primate, you won't die so easily.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.410
Haruto...

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:04.020
Dad, I made up my mind.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.410
Actually I've decided this a long time ago.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:08.910
What?

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.590
I'm going to destroy the Valvraves.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:15.670
I'll make it as if they never existed.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:24.440
Cut that out, Haruto! You're the embodiment of my very dreams!

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:28.670
Do you want to stop the progress of evolution and deny mankind its future?!

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:29.310
Enough.

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.680
Wait!

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:34.910
What's this all of a sudden? Isn't it going pretty well?

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:37.060
You're perfect!

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:40.870
Bye, Dad.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:07.140
Why?

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:09.370
Why?!

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:12.820
This isn't the same as it was three years ago.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:14.500
This time, I prepared a path.

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:17.520
I have a country for us to run to,

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:20.620
Lieselotte.

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.030
Mikhail...

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:33.790
Let me take you away.

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:15.430
PREVIEW

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:18.810
Next time, episode 19: Tears Like Falling Snow.

00:24:19.490 --> 00:24:24.480
Valvrave the Liberator... The system that unveils the world.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.980
EPISODE 19

